{"id":"591bf3d05e777f12ff3522aeaee67d74bdbf2c642639eb6e92c3ae8530f5480a","pubkey":"16d114303d8203115918ca34a220e925c022c09168175a5ace5e9f3b61640947","created_at":1781656160,"content":"https://nostr.download/267fcbde08f3139b3776b6898822ae25082d1999aab7ad56318f4abc2d2f97bb.jpg\nMercy is easy.\nThe fear of God is harder.\n\nFaith can comfort you. It can strengthen you. It can lift your mind out of despair.\n\nBut the deeper test is not whether belief makes life feel better.\n\nThe deeper test is whether it makes you truthful.\n\nMercy is the open door.\nFear of God is the discipline to walk through it changed.\n\nNot panic.\nNot superstition.\nNot religious performance.\n\nThe fear of God is moral gravity.\n\nIt is the moment the soul realizes truth is not negotiable, conscience is not decoration, and grace is not permission to keep lying to yourself.\n\nComfort is good.\nMercy is beautiful.\nBut reverence is what stops mercy becoming self-help.\n\nTry God, yes.\n\nBut do not only ask whether He works for you.\n\nAsk whether you are willing to let Him work on you.\n\n#Mercy #FearOfGod #Faith #Grace #Truth #Repentance #Christ #Conscience #MoralGravity #SpiritualDiscipline"}
