{"id":"2627bf1f310719204245f0af83827a2e20521da2a6f17863a28afeb4f8b431ae","pubkey":"d0ed1eb980bb9d178771f52df71dfcf38264d431d2c1bb3df14b278532cbb8ba","created_at":1781633698,"content":"Next up on my project was a web page for Clan Kincaid.  I contacted the the President of the society and got things rolling.  Us Kincaid's were fortunate to have a real Internet pioneer in Grant Kinkead of Melbourne, Australia.  His company Alphalink was part of the second wave of startups there.  He was kind enough to host my initial web site for free as well as my later kyncades.org site and a new Clan Kincaid web site and the Kincaid DNA project.  Grant also gave valuable help with the look of the first Clan Kincaid web pages.\n\nThere was a real problem with others stealing research (much like AI bots today) from the beginning.  One fellow copied my material word for word on his Great Hall of the Clans website.  By chance he lived in the same city as me so he was obliged to remove my content when I confronted him.\n\nPeter\n\n===============================\n\nReceived: ; Tue Jun 06 17:09:22 1995 -0300X-Priority: 3\nX-MSMail-Priority: Normal\nTo: <whk@umich.edu>\nX-MimeOLE: Produced By Microsoft MimeOLE V6.0.6000.16386\nFrom: \"Peter A. Kincaid\" <kincaidp@nbnet.nb.ca>\nSubject: Clan Kincaid\nCc: \nBcc: \nX-Attachments: \nX-EsetId: 795EA9210D2422322B1F\nX-EsetScannerBuild: 9204\n\nI noticed from a posting on soc.genealogy.misc that Clan Kincaid is online.  It is great to see us on the net.  If you recall I sent a letter to you regarding this subject.\n\nI have set up and am maintaining a WWW home page relating to genealogy and my part of the world (http://degaulle.hil.unb.ca/genealogy/nbgen.html).  If you ever consider putting together a Kincaid family home page I could help with putting together the HTML pages.  We would need to find a server to host it on though.\n\nBecause of my presence on the net, I get a number of queries from Kincaid descendants looking for info.  Most a related to early US Kincaids (ie. Virginia, etc).  I send them what I have if it helps and I have encouraged them to join our Clan society.  I suspect that you would have a lot of information available to you that would help these people.  Would you be able to either a) send me some of the most reliable documents so I can forward information on to these people or/and b) be interested in being part of a mailing list of Kincaid researchers who would want to help people with these queries (ie. a query is sent to all on the list and whoever can help would respond).\n\nI think it would also be good if we can get together a number of people who would want to donate time/money to research the origins of some of the main Kincaid lines and have that well documented information available to all members.  For example, there seems to be some suggested but unsourced claims to the Kincaid origins.  Royal charters should clearly state who the original grantees were for the Kincaid lands in Scotland.  Land registry information would also show a chain of title for these lands to the present day, thus indicating the line of the Lairdship.  This would be great information to have searched and made available.  The claim that William Francis was a Kincaid also needs to be sourced.  There also appears to be uncertainty over the first couple of generation of the early Virginia Kincaids.  I am currently trying to sort though the Irish Kincaid line which I come from and will make this available when done, although I could use some help with the costs.\n\nI think these are some great projects which the Clan Kincaid society could address and which the Internet could play a great role with.  I am willing to help in any way I can.  I would be interested in hearing your thoughts.\n\nBTW, have you been able to find copies of Issues 11, 12, and 13 of the Clan Kincaid newsletter.  I would like to get copies.  Furthermore, any word on when the next issue will be out.\n\n\n\n\nReceived: ; Tue May 28 17:47:27 1996 -0300\nX-Priority: 3X-MSMail-Priority: Normal\nTo: <K-Fen>\nX-MimeOLE: Produced By Microsoft MimeOLE V6.0.6000.16386\nFrom: \"Peter A. Kincaid\" <kincaidp@mi.net>\nSubject: It's ready!! (The Clan Kincaid WWW Page)\nCc: \nBcc: \nX-Attachments: \nOld-X-EsetId: 5F623320F4A433370C26\nX-EsetScannerBuild: 9204\nX-EsetId: 795EA9210D2422322B1F\n\nHello everyone!\n\nWell the Clan Kincaid World Wide Web (WWW) home page is now ready for viewing.  Its URL is:\n\nhttp://www.alphalink.com.au/ind.htm\n\nPlease forward your comments to me as I appreciate your input.  I'd like to wait a little bit before going public; in case some of you notice some errors.\n\nNow.  We should all give our sincerest thanks to Grant Kinkead and Alphalink for hosting the page and for Grant's work at making the page look as great as it does.  He has done some super work on the color schemes and graphics.  It has been a pleasure working with him.  Thanks Grant!!\n\n\n\n"}
