{"id":"6e3120e111b704fa9e2d6e67dc18e779ad4060c2f9bc9538e4c62a28038d3373","pubkey":"d0ed1eb980bb9d178771f52df71dfcf38264d431d2c1bb3df14b278532cbb8ba","created_at":1781629892,"content":"From an old email announcing to a group my recent launch of the New Brunswick Genealogy Information Page ~32 years ago.  This was one of the earlier personal use HTML web pages in Canada.  I worked with Stephen Sloan to set this up on a server at Harriet Irving Library on the UNB campus in Fredericton.  I coded the pages and telnet it to an account he set up for me there.  I hope to post some old email relating to this another time.\n\nPeter\n\nP.S. All the links are long dead\n==================================\n\nFrom: kincaidp@nbnet.nb.ca (Peter A. Kincaid)\nSubject: ANNOUNCE: New Brunswick Genealogical Information Page\nDate: Thu, 17 Nov 1994 21:41:41 UNDEFINED\n\nA new WWW Home Page is now available for those researching their ancestors\nfrom New Brunswick, Canada.  Called the New Brunswick Genealogical Information\nPage this URL site lists sources of genealogical data in New Brunswick.  \nInformation on material available as well as addresses for these sources are \nprovided.  The URL is:\n\nhttp://www.unb.ca/genealogy/nbgen.html\n\nThis page is made available thanks to the support of the Harriet Irving  Library\non the University of New Brunswick campus in Fredericton, New Brunswick.\n\nIn the future this Home Page will list other sources as well as provide \nfinding aids for genealogical material housed at the Provincial Archives.  It \nis hoped that in the near future this Page will include searchable indexes of \nearly New Brunswick families (ie. Land petitions indexes, Census records \nindexes, etc).\n\nYour comments and suggestions regarding this new Home Page are welcomed.\n\n\nPeter A. Kincaid\nFredericton, NB, Canada\nkincaidp@nbnet.nb.ca\n"}
