{"id":"2dda63dda767e378c34436fe51a68e7bea8904a275bace81b9e4bf3c1084e448","pubkey":"19f9afb8f855f5e86b5bea160e78ec5871648b10dedb043f4806fca8ce50e4d3","created_at":1781623237,"content":"GM!\n#rupertsbackyardtoday is mostly back yard with a little front yard thrown in for lagniappe. And because the back yard only has so much going on sometimes. \n\nFruit and flower, these passion fruit vines are so cool. I wonder if the leaves are edible...time for research. \nhttps://cdn.satellite.earth/64b153ea9e5fec3dcd0c05b9a1d276e5ef3afc14d2c903722d6a8b15801d1032.jpg\n\nWent lookin' for froggos and found a rolypoly instead. Good enough.\nhttps://cdn.satellite.earth/865b01e97baac20d008c3935af1bfbf75342980a6cc707b0304ddabeae93eb0b.jpg\n\nCoriander berries and an inkcap hanging out among the cilantro plants.\nhttps://cdn.satellite.earth/57ae13eb37eb629d7d9a53fa505e3215ba75477f89376abdf79ae3ccab36a375.jpg\n\nI guarantee this is the smallest fig you've ever seen or your entry fee to #rupertsbackyardtoday will be refunded.\nhttps://cdn.satellite.earth/50d70a1fce98fccf4b006bd654bc5b06c3bfbc2b42582e3a00e4548125c1f202.jpg\n\nFront yard inspections revealed that some scrawny caterpillar got buff on my hostas. Last pic is dna evidence left at the scene by the perp, aka caterpillar poops.\nhttps://cdn.satellite.earth/b637b2abe4acb7c116511e81f76748f7ae4fa79f3f465a9e992c39455c2669a0.jpg\n\nBabies and thick bois and buds!\nhttps://cdn.satellite.earth/6f7fa10ff7512c2e66dd12b1cdc90d71dc45b6d593978bbb536e5fae339652ab.jpg\n\nBecause we didn't find froggos this morning, have a couple big fellers from last night.\nhttps://cdn.satellite.earth/330b35e309e4201f3963615762cd52facf4882d83fcf95233ed41a5911107539.jpg https://cdn.satellite.earth/33146f69707a52839ef60693c026aaa59e6e510b861e5907388ecb291acd228b.jpg\n\n#iguessilladdrealhashtagsthistime #naturestr #bloomstr #gardenstr #plantstr #frogstr #frogup"}
